{"id":"bf878a9b9d805cfb79cfaee93dcc6100baea1b69","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"bf878a9b9d805cfb79cfaee93dcc6100baea1b69","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/pnpr-metrics-need-a-token-or-listener.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/pnpr\": minor","+---","+","+pnpr serves Prometheus metrics at `/-/metrics` and `/metrics` only when the config has a `metrics` block. Before, it served them to anyone.","+","+Set `metrics.token` to require a bearer token from the scraper. Set `metrics.listen` to serve metrics on a separate address, such as one on a private network, and not on the main address."],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/config.yaml","lines":["@@ -21,6 +21,11 @@ storage: ./storage"," #  - 10.0.0.0/8"," #trustedProxyHeader: x-forwarded-for"," ","+# Prometheus metrics (not served unless this block is present).","+#metrics:","+#  token: ${PNPR_METRICS_TOKEN}   # scrapers send it as a bearer token","+#  listen: 127.0.0.1:9464         # serve metrics only on this address","+"," # S3-compatible object store for hosted packages."," #s3:"," #  bucket: my-pnpr-packages"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/config_file.rs","lines":["@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@"," use super::{","     AccessSpec, ByteSize, Deserialize, Ecosystem, IndexMap, Interval, LogConfig, LogFormat,","-    LogLevel, Management, OciConfig, PackageAccess, PathBuf, S3Settings, ScimConfig, TarballFormat,","-    UpstreamAuthFile, default_storage_string, oidc,","+    LogLevel, Management, MetricsConfig, OciConfig, PackageAccess, PathBuf, S3Settings, ScimConfig,","+    TarballFormat, UpstreamAuthFile, default_storage_string, oidc,"," };"," "," /// Disk shape of the `routes:` block.","@@ -235,6 +235,9 @@ pub(super) struct ConfigFile {","     pub(super) ui: UiFile,","     #[serde(default)]","     pub(super) oci: OciConfig,","+    /// Who may scrape Prometheus metrics. Omitted ⇒ pnpr serves none.","+    #[serde(default)]","+    pub(super) metrics: Option<MetricsConfig>,","     /// pnpr-only block: store the hosted (published) packages in an","     /// S3-compatible object store instead of `storage`.","     #[serde(default)]"],"additions":5,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ pub use byte_size::{ByteSize, parse_byte_size};"," pub use hosted::{HostedConfig, Management};"," pub use ip_network::{IpNetwork, parse_trusted_proxies};"," pub use logging::{LogConfig, LogFormat, LogLevel};","+pub use metrics::MetricsConfig;"," pub use pnpr_policy::{TeamDirectory, Teams};"," pub use s3::{HostedStoreConfig, S3Settings, build_s3_store, normalize_key_prefix};"," pub use scim::ScimConfig;","@@ -53,6 +54,8 @@ mod loading;"," mod logging;"," use logging::build_log_config;"," ","+mod metrics;","+"," mod registry_graph;"," use registry_graph::{","     ResolvedFileRegistries, org_collision_error, registry_err, resolve_file_registries,","@@ -205,10 +208,21 @@ pub struct HttpConfig {","     /// this duration to process, it is aborted and returns 504 Gateway Timeout.","     /// `None` or 0 disables request timeouts.","     pub request_timeout: Option<Duration>,","+    /// Who may scrape Prometheus metrics. `None` serves none.","+    pub metrics: Option<MetricsConfig>,"," }"," "," impl HttpConfig {","     pub const DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_mins(1);","+","+    /// The checks config loading applies to `metrics`, for a config built in","+    /// code.","+    pub fn ensure_valid_metrics(&self) -> Result<(), RegistryError> {","+        match &self.metrics {","+            Some(metrics) => metrics.validate(self.listen),","+            None => Ok(()),","+        }","+    }"," }"," "," #[derive(Debug, Clone)]"],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/loading.rs","lines":["@@ -303,9 +303,21 @@ fn build_http_config(","         trusted_proxies,","         trusted_proxy_header,","         request_timeout,","+        metrics: build_metrics_config(file, listen)?,","     })"," }"," ","+fn build_metrics_config(","+    file: &mut ConfigFile,","+    listen: SocketAddr,","+) -> Result<Option<super::MetricsConfig>, RegistryError> {","+    let metrics = file.metrics.take();","+    if let Some(metrics) = &metrics {","+        metrics.validate(listen)?;","+    }","+    Ok(metrics)","+}","+"," fn build_storage_config(","     file: &mut ConfigFile,","     base_dir: &Path,"],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/metrics.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@","+use pnpr_error::RegistryError;","+use serde::Deserialize;","+use std::{fmt, net::SocketAddr};","+","+/// The YAML `metrics:` block. pnpr serves Prometheus metrics only when it is","+/// present, and only to a scraper that holds `token` or reaches `listen`.","+#[derive(Clone, Deserialize)]","+#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]","+pub struct MetricsConfig {","+    /// The bearer secret a scraper sends.","+    #[serde(default)]","+    pub token: Option<String>,","+    /// The address of a listener that serves only metrics. When set, the main","+    /// listener does not serve them.","+    #[serde(default)]","+    pub listen: Option<SocketAddr>,","+}","+","+impl MetricsConfig {","+    /// The shortest `token` pnpr accepts, not counting surrounding whitespace.","+    pub const MIN_TOKEN_LEN: usize = 32;","+","+    pub(super) fn validate(&self, server_listen: SocketAddr) -> Result<(), RegistryError> {","+        match (&self.token, self.listen) {","+            (None, None) => Err(RegistryError::InvalidConfig {","+                reason: \"metrics needs a token, a listen address, or both\".to_string(),","+            }),","+            (_, Some(listen)) if binds_overlap(listen, server_listen) => {","+                Err(RegistryError::InvalidConfig {","+                    reason: format!(","+                        \"metrics.listen {listen} takes the port of the server's listen address {server_listen}\",","+                    ),","+                })","+            }","+            (Some(token), _) if token.trim().chars().count() < Self::MIN_TOKEN_LEN => {","+                Err(RegistryError::InvalidConfig {","+                    reason: format!(","+                        \"metrics.token must be at least {} characters long\",","+                        Self::MIN_TOKEN_LEN,","+                    ),","+                })","+            }","+            _ => Ok(()),","+        }","+    }","+}","+","+/// Whether binding both addresses would collide: the same port, unless it is","+/// the OS-assigned port 0, on the same address or with either one a wildcard.","+fn binds_overlap(left: SocketAddr, right: SocketAddr) -> bool {","+    left.port() != 0","+        && left.port() == right.port()","+        && (left.ip() == right.ip() || left.ip().is_unspecified() || right.ip().is_unspecified())","+}","+","+impl fmt::Debug for MetricsConfig {","+    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {","+        f.debug_struct(\"MetricsConfig\")","+            .field(\"token\", &self.token.as_ref().map(|_| \"<redacted>\"))","+            .field(\"listen\", &self.listen)","+            .finish()","+    }","+}"],"additions":63,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/secrets.rs","lines":["@@ -139,6 +139,9 @@ fn validate_auth_secrets<Sys: EnvVar>(val: &serde_json::Value) -> Result<(), Reg","     if let Some(token) = val.pointer(\"/auth/scim/token\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str) {","         check_secret_env_field::<Sys>(\"auth.scim.token\", token)?;","     }","+    if let Some(token) = val.pointer(\"/metrics/token\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str) {","+        check_secret_env_field::<Sys>(\"metrics.token\", token)?;","+    }","     let Some(oidc) = val.pointer(\"/auth/oidc\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_array) else {","         return Ok(());","     };"],"additions":3,"deletions"